  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If a player travels at high speed (~40 m/s or 90 mph) somewhere in a map *even if it isn't into a trigger volume*, the OnPlayerTriggerEnter event's reliability decreases for other trigger volumes when the player enters them at any speed. Once this missed event happens to a player, it becomes more frequent until all instances of the event stop working across multiple scripts. The effect is not uniform for all players, but it seems to be random and unrelated to PC hardware performance.\n\nExample:\n\nIn the Qoo H. Bocuma Airport world, if a player travels from one terminal to another using the train or the BHS, the likelihood of OnPlayerTriggerEnter events being dropped appears to increase with the amount of distance the player has traveled in the world. There appears to be a \"cascade\" effect where once an OnPlayerTriggerEnter event gets dropped, the likelihood of subsequent drops increases once it happens to a player.",
